./LOGBOOK.md:527:- DECISION: keep `manager-worker-v1`; do not mint `manager-worker-v2`. The two lower graph nodes were always per-operation values bound by the toolchain identity inside the build input, never constants of the policy, so restating them generically changes no `go-v1` byte. Minting a new identity would change every `go-v1` cache key and invalidate the frozen rc.5 candidate for zero security gain. Verified: regeneration byte-identical, pin still `sha256:9ba9b8ec…`.
