nstead of parallel maps, observation.current() is the single recheck door and re-reads through the reader that recorded the entry, and the four declaration keys have their own documentKey type - a document can only enter through observeDocument, which takes a generation, and cannot be passed to observe, which takes a path, so reintroducing the ABA-prone form is a compile error. TESTS: 10 new permanent cases. internal/install/generation_test.go locks the binding at the read for both writer shapes (in-place rewrite mid-read, and rename mid-read where the payload stays on the old inode and the recheck must see the replacement), plus content-addressing, absent, unreadable stability, and a direct recheck case. internal/install/aba_test.go drives the full A to B to A sequence through each documents real writer for project manifest, global manifest, hand-edited substitutions and hybrid activation: each asserts the restoration was byte-identical, requires the restart to name its observation, and proves no transient context, shim, adapter mirror, marker substituted field or consumer state committed and no journal survived. The transient generation is applied inside the single read through a one-shot afterDocumentOpen seam, nil in production, same convention as godriver.controlSeamFault; the seam fails the test if the window never opened. A byte-identical-rewrite control proves the fix does not turn every concurrent save into a restart. NEGATIVE CONTROL both orderings: with digest-before-read restored all four install-level ABA cases FAIL and fail by committing the transient declaration (skill-b installed, SUBSTITUTED recorded, hybrid skill-h installed, no restart message) and the in-place binding case fails while the control still passes; with the digest taken after the read the rename binding case fails. GATES on the final tree 19:50-20:08, standalone processes with durable exits: gofmt 0, diff-check 0, build 0, vet 0, test-r5 0 (15s), test-revalidation 0 (30s, the 6 R4 cases), test-loaders 0, reviewer cycle-2 hybrid and cycle-3 project/global repro overlays 0 unmodified, test-install 0 (190s), test-atomicity 0 (406s), test-rest 0 (29s), five race gates 0 with zero data races, pinned golangci-lint v2.4.0 repo-wide 0 issues and re-confirmed 0 after cache clean. NOT CLAIMED: test-godriver exited 1 (51s) on one subtest hitting the sibling-owned 15.02s wall-clock probe deadline with no assertion failure under load average 12+; isolated rerun of the same tree exits 0 in 28s. The cycle-4 ABA overlay is NOT re-runnable and is not claimed: it pins a pre-R5 copy of install.go and its two hook points name a window this fix deletes; that scenario is now a permanent test whose negative control reproduces the reviewer failure exactly. REVIEWER ATTENTION: two deliberate behaviour changes fall out of digesting bytes instead of a path - a chmod no longer restarts a run, and a symlinked manifest is now revalidated by content, where DigestPath previously refused the link and pinned it to an unreadable marker that compared equal to itself forever, i.e. a symlinked manifest was not revalidated at all. Darwin/arm64 only; hardened containment STORY-260728-327soo remains separate and non-gating and is not claimed.
